  "notes": "Describes the Moroccan-administered area, where most of the territory's learners live and schools run under Morocco's education ministry through its regional academies, so it mirrors Morocco's system: six years of primary, three of collège, then the common core and two baccalaureate years. Schools of the Sahrawi refugee camps near Tindouf (Algeria) and the Polisario-held area follow another system and are left out. Unconfirmed: the entry age of six and the year names come from Moroccan national pages, not from pages about the territory."
